WEBVTT

00:09.093 --> 00:12.345
Silvermane.
In charge of organize crime for 30 years.

00:12.346 --> 00:15.181
Someone burned down his mansion
a couple of nights ago.

00:15.182 --> 00:17.267
-  Addison!
- You keep following me,

00:17.268 --> 00:18.685
it won't end the way you want it to.

00:18.686 --> 00:20.770
This guy have superpowers?
Like you?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.607
Do me favor. Hold off on printing that.

00:24.608 --> 00:26.901
I want to warn Donegal
before he gets himself killed.

00:26.902 --> 00:28.361
That's enough of that.

00:28.362 --> 00:29.863
There's gonna be a free-for-all.

00:29.864 --> 00:31.865
The people could use a hero.

00:31.866 --> 00:33.491
I hope they find someone.

00:33.492 --> 00:36.327
I can't help but wonder
what Ruby would think.

00:36.328 --> 00:37.829
I'm not that guy anymore.

00:37.830 --> 00:39.372
Any chance

00:39.373 --> 00:40.373
you know who this is?

00:40.374 --> 00:41.416
Oh, that's Cat Hardy.

00:41.417 --> 00:43.084
Star attraction over at The Alcove.

00:43.085 --> 00:44.586
Is there somewhere we can talk?

00:44.587 --> 00:45.712
- It's business.
- Flint.

00:45.713 --> 00:46.755
Despite what I do,

00:46.756 --> 00:48.006
I don't enjoy hurting people.

00:52.720 --> 00:55.180
- Don't hurt him.
- What the hell is this?

00:55.181 --> 00:57.640
- Just leave us alone, please.
-  When someone

00:57.641 --> 00:58.725
tells you what they are,

00:58.726 --> 01:00.643
- you have to listen.
-  And what is he?

01:00.644 --> 01:02.604
Retired.

01:02.605 --> 01:04.147
I came here to offer him a job.

01:04.148 --> 01:06.859
My friend you met last night--
he's disappeared.

01:34.178 --> 01:35.303
You were saying Flint's your bodyguard.

01:35.304 --> 01:38.556
Yes. He protects me and he is loyal.

01:38.557 --> 01:40.099
Hard to find these days.

01:40.100 --> 01:42.936
No kidding. I didn't marry my husband
for his looks.

01:42.937 --> 01:45.939
What else can you tell us?
Does he have family, friends?

01:45.940 --> 01:48.191
I don't know anything
about his personal life.

01:48.192 --> 01:49.693
I know his address.

01:50.778 --> 01:53.989
Are we gonna talk about the fact that
he turned into some kind of sand monster?

01:55.783 --> 01:57.076
What I know, she knows.

01:58.410 --> 02:00.245
It started about six months ago.

02:00.246 --> 02:02.247
Slow, at first.

02:02.248 --> 02:04.332
But it's been getting worse.

02:04.333 --> 02:06.668
And he never remembers when it happens?

02:06.669 --> 02:08.336
Oh, he always remembers.

02:08.337 --> 02:11.214
Unless he gets clubbed in the head
with an iron girder.

02:12.341 --> 02:15.802
That's it? He turned into sand. That's--
It was sand, right?

02:15.803 --> 02:17.387
Just seems like kind of, like, a big deal.

02:17.388 --> 02:20.390
So, do you have any clues
as to what's causing this to happen?

02:20.391 --> 02:21.933
You haven't given us much to go on.

02:21.934 --> 02:23.810
Isn't that what the money's for?

02:23.811 --> 02:25.436
You're an investigator.

02:25.437 --> 02:27.231
Investigate.

02:28.232 --> 02:30.191
You know, an artist
doesn't just paint with air.

02:30.192 --> 02:32.735
He needs a canvas, brushes, paint.

02:32.736 --> 02:35.154
Do you think I'm withholding
from you, Mr. Reilly?

02:35.155 --> 02:36.447
What if I said I did?

02:36.448 --> 02:37.782
I'd ask why you thought that.

02:37.783 --> 02:39.826
- I'd say a lifetime of experience.
- With clients?

02:39.827 --> 02:41.828
With… women.

02:43.289 --> 02:45.164
As fun as this little game is, I'm afraid

02:45.165 --> 02:47.584
I have other business to attend to.

02:47.585 --> 02:49.587
Get to painting, Mr. Reilly.

02:58.721 --> 03:00.054
What do you think?

03:00.055 --> 03:02.390
I think you might need a cold shower.

03:02.391 --> 03:03.893
I think I might need one.

03:06.270 --> 03:08.146
But you're right.

03:08.147 --> 03:09.898
She is hiding something.

03:09.899 --> 03:11.150
All the fun ones do.

03:11.817 --> 03:13.568
I'm gonna check out Flint's apartment.

03:13.569 --> 03:14.819
Why don't you do down to the Bu--

03:14.820 --> 03:17.530
Bureau of Criminal Records? Yeah.

03:17.531 --> 03:19.449
Been a while since we've had a real case.

03:19.450 --> 03:20.784
But it ain't been that long.

03:23.537 --> 03:26.164
♪ You got to accentuate ♪

03:26.165 --> 03:28.249
♪ the positive ♪

03:28.250 --> 03:30.919
♪ eliminate the negative ♪

03:30.920 --> 03:34.839
♪ and latch on to the affirmative ♪

03:34.840 --> 03:38.009
♪ Don't mess with Mr. In-Between ♪

03:38.010 --> 03:40.428
♪ You got to spread joy ♪

03:40.429 --> 03:42.347
♪ up to the maximum ♪

03:42.348 --> 03:45.808
♪ bring gloom down to the minimum ♪

03:45.809 --> 03:47.894
- ♪ and have faith ♪
- ♪ Amen ♪

03:47.895 --> 03:49.729
♪ or pandemonium's ♪

03:49.730 --> 03:51.941
♪ liable to walk upon the scene ♪

03:53.442 --> 03:54.859
♪ Amen ♪

04:01.450 --> 04:04.286
Gonna meet a new supplier
at the docks tomorrow.

04:05.454 --> 04:06.913
Canadian.

04:06.914 --> 04:08.331
You didn't tell me that.

04:08.332 --> 04:09.750
I'm telling you now.

04:11.043 --> 04:14.754
It's not smart for you to go out in public
till we know who tried to take you out.

04:14.755 --> 04:16.506
I'll go where I want.

04:16.507 --> 04:19.175
With all due respect,
you don't pay me what you pay me

04:19.176 --> 04:21.135
for my charm or disposition.

04:21.136 --> 04:25.098
You pay me to keep you alive
and I'm telling you it's a bad idea.

04:25.099 --> 04:28.726
If you dying benefitted me,
I would have done it myself ten years ago.

04:28.727 --> 04:31.187
But I know what I'm good at,
I know what I'm not,

04:31.188 --> 04:34.107
and I need you to stay alive and in power.

04:34.108 --> 04:36.776
So, pretty please, with cherries on top,

04:36.777 --> 04:38.319
let me go down to the docks ahead of you.

04:38.320 --> 04:40.530
Once I make sure everything's kosher,
you can waltz on in

04:40.531 --> 04:42.533
and show everyone
the brightness of your feathers.

04:43.534 --> 04:45.035
You finished?

04:48.706 --> 04:50.456
Problem is not that the guy is out there.

04:50.457 --> 04:53.710
The problem is they thought
they could take me out at all.

04:53.711 --> 04:56.170
Ever since The Spider disappeared,

04:56.171 --> 04:58.131
things have been comfortable.

04:58.132 --> 05:01.259
Maybe someone's thinking
that I got complacent.

05:01.260 --> 05:02.761
Or soft.

05:03.679 --> 05:04.763
Maybe you're one of them.

05:06.557 --> 05:08.474
Thinking you could take me out.

05:08.475 --> 05:10.810
If you could set yourself on fire

05:10.811 --> 05:13.229
like Addison, then you might have a shot.

05:13.230 --> 05:16.482
Imagine controlling that kind of power.

05:16.483 --> 05:19.027
Now Flint goes missing.

05:19.028 --> 05:20.611
Right after.

05:20.612 --> 05:23.364
He's been acting strange lately.

05:23.365 --> 05:25.659
And if those two things are related...

05:26.577 --> 05:27.661
Go look for Flint.

05:32.416 --> 05:34.667
And when the boys find that PI...

05:34.668 --> 05:36.002
Reilly.

05:36.003 --> 05:37.504
Bring him straight to me.

05:53.270 --> 05:55.938
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

05:55.939 --> 05:57.690
♪ I could tell the story ♪

05:57.691 --> 06:00.359
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

06:00.360 --> 06:03.154
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

06:03.155 --> 06:05.239
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

06:05.240 --> 06:07.700
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

06:07.701 --> 06:10.912
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

06:10.913 --> 06:14.248
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

06:14.249 --> 06:17.376
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

06:17.377 --> 06:20.838
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

06:20.839 --> 06:24.050
♪ Hey, lover ♪

06:24.051 --> 06:26.928
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

06:26.929 --> 06:29.180
♪ from all the pain ♪

06:29.181 --> 06:31.641
♪ I suffer ♪

06:31.642 --> 06:34.477
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

06:34.478 --> 06:38.022
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

06:38.023 --> 06:40.399
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

06:40.400 --> 06:41.776
♪ But you could be ♪

06:41.777 --> 06:44.988
♪ my saving grace ♪

07:34.705 --> 07:35.956
Great.

07:47.426 --> 07:48.509
Hi, this is

07:48.510 --> 07:50.511
- Robbie Robertson calling.
-  Mr. Robertson,

07:50.512 --> 07:53.848
how many times do I have to tell you?
You're never getting your old job back.

07:53.849 --> 07:56.893
Listen, I don't know if Walters
has seen my article in the Gazette,

07:56.894 --> 07:59.270
- but I just-- I--
- Mr. Robertson, there's no point...

07:59.271 --> 08:01.772
What I'm saying is I j--
I-I just need to sit with him, that's all.

08:01.773 --> 08:04.400
- Mr. Roberston, please. Mr. Robertson,
- But if you-if you just...

08:04.401 --> 08:06.652
- I'm going to hang up now.
- ...you would just give me a chance to--

08:06.653 --> 08:08.779
I'm onto something truly sensational!

08:08.780 --> 08:10.323
It's the biggest story in years.

08:10.324 --> 08:12.576
There hasn't been anything this big
since The Spider.

08:15.162 --> 08:17.998
I promise it'll be worth his while.

08:21.627 --> 08:23.462
I'll see what I can do.

08:25.422 --> 08:27.924
Thank you. Thank you.

08:29.092 --> 08:32.178
Flint Marko?

08:32.179 --> 08:34.305
Got a delivery.

08:34.306 --> 08:35.932
Anybody home?

08:35.933 --> 08:37.183
Come on...

09:21.812 --> 09:23.689
Flint.

09:27.526 --> 09:29.236
Addison!

09:32.864 --> 09:34.740
Flint.

09:34.741 --> 09:37.369
It's Winston.
Silvermane wants to talk to you.

09:38.370 --> 09:40.538
Gimme the keys.

09:52.551 --> 09:54.261
Check the bedroom.

10:46.855 --> 10:48.565
Nice place.

10:50.484 --> 10:53.194
Yeah. Bit fancy for my taste.

10:53.195 --> 10:56.364
And I got a pretty good idea why.

10:56.365 --> 10:57.449
Why?

10:58.325 --> 10:59.700
Let's go.

10:59.701 --> 11:01.243
You think he got a new lady?

11:01.244 --> 11:04.080
That why he ain't coming to poker lately?

11:11.046 --> 11:14.090
♪ If you're blue and you don't know
where to go to ♪

11:14.091 --> 11:17.927
♪ why don't you go where fashion sits? ♪

11:17.928 --> 11:19.887
♪ Puttin' on the Ritz...

11:19.888 --> 11:22.723
Janet. Long time.

11:22.724 --> 11:24.100
Thought you might've wised up
and quit the biz.

11:24.101 --> 11:25.976
Oh, no, not me, Hank.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.063
Sad to report I'm dumb as ever.

11:29.523 --> 11:31.524
Found this sitting outside.

11:31.525 --> 11:33.359
I didn't know if it belonged to anyone.

11:33.360 --> 11:34.944
Hmm.

11:34.945 --> 11:36.821
♪ with their swell beaus...

11:36.822 --> 11:38.948
Ooh.

11:38.949 --> 11:40.950
You know my wife
made me quit eating these.

11:40.951 --> 11:42.159
Okay, well, in that case...

11:42.160 --> 11:45.204
Hey! Last I checked, you ain't my wife.

11:45.205 --> 11:46.956
♪ Puttin' on the Ritz...

11:46.957 --> 11:49.208
- Name?
- Flint Marko.

11:49.209 --> 11:51.001
All right. Be right back.

11:51.002 --> 11:52.461
Don't you dare touch that bag.

11:52.462 --> 11:54.797
It ain't a bribe if I don't get to eat it.

11:54.798 --> 11:56.590
♪ Puttin' on ♪

11:56.591 --> 11:57.758
-  Janet, good to see you.
- ♪ the Ritz...! ♪

11:57.759 --> 11:59.761
Oh! Hey, Charlie. How you been?

12:03.056 --> 12:06.016
Quite the record, our Mr. Marko.

12:06.017 --> 12:09.353
Grew up in Brooklyn. Working class.
Came back with no prospects.

12:09.354 --> 12:11.605
Small crimes, then bigger ones.

12:11.606 --> 12:14.191
Arrest, arrest, arrest.

12:14.192 --> 12:16.152
Now an enforcer for--

12:16.153 --> 12:17.778
Silvermane.

12:17.779 --> 12:20.157
That Winston guy showed up
while I was at Flint's.

12:20.866 --> 12:23.326
- You hid in the closet?
- I hid in the closet.

12:25.078 --> 12:26.454
Meuse-Argonne.

12:26.455 --> 12:28.289
Didn't you fight there too?

12:28.290 --> 12:30.833
Yeah.
Was one of the biggest battles of the war.

12:30.834 --> 12:32.168
There were a million of us there.

12:32.169 --> 12:35.212
- Hold on. Is that--
- Addison.

12:35.213 --> 12:36.755
Looks like they were in the war together.

12:36.756 --> 12:39.300
Is that what Cat is hiding from you?

12:39.301 --> 12:42.094
I bet she knew that Flint
had a friend with superpowers.

12:42.095 --> 12:44.930
Oh, I know. What I don't know
is why she didn't tell me.

12:44.931 --> 12:46.765
Probably thought
you wouldn't have taken the case.

12:46.766 --> 12:48.642
She would've been right.

13:24.304 --> 13:26.180
I don't think I've ever heard that one.

13:26.181 --> 13:28.015
I wouldn't think so.

13:28.016 --> 13:29.518
It's an original.

13:31.895 --> 13:34.189
Visited Flint's apartment today.

13:36.733 --> 13:38.275
This mean anything to you?

13:38.276 --> 13:40.569
I knew he was in the war.

13:40.570 --> 13:43.113
Hard to believe he was ever so young.

13:43.114 --> 13:44.907
What about this guy?

13:44.908 --> 13:46.492
You see him--
this little guy, right over here?

13:46.493 --> 13:49.496
He ever come around The Alcove,
visit Marko?

13:50.956 --> 13:52.457
Can't say I've ever seen him.

13:53.833 --> 13:56.961
His name's... Addison.

13:56.962 --> 13:59.755
He's the guy that
burned down Silvermane's mansion.

13:59.756 --> 14:01.590
He's dead now.

14:01.591 --> 14:03.343
So's the PI that shot him.

14:03.927 --> 14:07.638
What can I say?
The world's a dangerous place.

14:12.102 --> 14:13.894
You're pretty cool under pressure.

14:13.895 --> 14:15.729
- I wasn't aware I was under any.
- Why didn't you tell me

14:15.730 --> 14:18.482
- Flint worked for Silvermane?
- Would you have taken the case if I had?

14:18.483 --> 14:19.483
- I don't like surprises.
- I'll remember that

14:19.484 --> 14:21.152
when your birthday rolls around.

14:24.406 --> 14:26.448
The deed is under my name,

14:26.449 --> 14:29.535
but it's no secret
Silvermane owns this place.

14:29.536 --> 14:32.454
And Flint's a good way
to protect his investment.

14:32.455 --> 14:34.457
- And you.
- And me.

14:35.750 --> 14:38.877
You see, this club lives and dies
on people walking through that door

14:38.878 --> 14:40.839
because they want what I give them.

14:44.175 --> 14:46.093
You trying to get me, Mr. Reilly?

14:46.094 --> 14:48.012
"Get you"?

14:48.013 --> 14:49.680
Understand me.

14:49.681 --> 14:51.181
Seems you got my number.

14:51.182 --> 14:53.309
I've learned a lot of them over the years.

14:53.310 --> 14:55.686
Oh, o-one for every Tom, Dick and Harry?

14:55.687 --> 14:58.147
Hmm. You're interesting.

14:58.148 --> 15:00.274
Oh, yeah? How's that?

15:00.275 --> 15:03.694
Well, the other night when we met,
you called yourself a coward.

15:03.695 --> 15:06.071
But I think you're braver than you let on.

15:06.072 --> 15:08.490
Oh you're good.

15:08.491 --> 15:10.743
In an obvious sort of way.

15:10.744 --> 15:12.620
I'm as subtle as the situation requires.

15:12.621 --> 15:15.039
You see, I have business with Silvermane

15:15.040 --> 15:17.124
and I have business with you, Mr. Reilly.

15:17.125 --> 15:18.959
One has nothing to do with the other.

15:18.960 --> 15:22.172
Now, have I said enough for you
to keep the money you came here to return?

15:23.256 --> 15:24.840
Or have I misjudged you?

15:24.841 --> 15:27.509
No I'll keep working the case.

15:27.510 --> 15:29.095
Not because I'm brave.

15:30.180 --> 15:31.555
- Why, then?
- Uh,

15:31.556 --> 15:33.807
a singer's got to know all the numbers.

15:33.808 --> 15:37.186
Maybe a detective has just
got to know all the answers.

16:33.993 --> 16:35.036
Uh...

16:37.080 --> 16:38.872
It's, uh...

16:38.873 --> 16:40.582
It.. Tai chi.

16:40.583 --> 16:42.292
Yeah, that's right. It's tai chi.

16:42.293 --> 16:43.794
It's, uh, it's good.

16:43.795 --> 16:47.339
It's good for breathing and relaxation.

16:47.340 --> 16:48.757
I recommend it.

16:50.051 --> 16:52.386
We don't have the slightest clue
what you're talking about.

16:52.387 --> 16:53.972
We don't care, either.

16:56.307 --> 16:58.143
Oh!

17:01.938 --> 17:03.856
A toaster? Really?

17:03.857 --> 17:05.941
Gosh, I shouldn't have thrown it so hard.

17:15.660 --> 17:18.537
-  Come on. Come on.
-  Let's go for a ride.

17:27.630 --> 17:29.548
Mind telling me why I'm here?

17:29.549 --> 17:31.008
Silvermane wants to see you.

17:31.009 --> 17:33.635
I figured that. I'm asking why.

17:33.636 --> 17:35.512
We're not really the "why" guys.

17:35.513 --> 17:38.474
Maybe you wouldn't be here
if you didn't try ripping the boss off.

17:38.475 --> 17:39.850
Ah, Donegal.

17:39.851 --> 17:41.268
I didn't have anything

17:41.269 --> 17:42.478
to do with his little scheme.

17:42.479 --> 17:44.146
I actually tried to talk him out of it.

17:44.147 --> 17:46.774
Like I said, the boss just wants to talk.

17:46.775 --> 17:50.444
And I've got no idea who hired Addison
to burn down your boss' house.

17:50.445 --> 17:52.112
You don't know nothing, huh?

17:52.113 --> 17:53.947
Double negative,
but we'll set that aside for now.

17:53.948 --> 17:55.657
My point is I'm not much of a detective.

17:55.658 --> 17:57.284
Yeah, then you got nothing to worry about.

17:57.285 --> 17:58.619
Just like Donegal, right?

17:58.620 --> 18:01.413
Yeah, just like Donegal.

18:01.414 --> 18:04.208
Uh, by the way, I am sorry about the nose.

18:04.209 --> 18:07.002
Me? That was him.

18:07.003 --> 18:08.796
Oh! Oh...

18:12.675 --> 18:14.511
Get out!

18:20.683 --> 18:22.267
Where'd he go?

18:22.268 --> 18:23.895
Check the side.

18:30.860 --> 18:32.444
The boss ain't gonna like this.

18:32.445 --> 18:34.447
Yeah, he wanted us to bring him in.

18:35.782 --> 18:37.616
Get in the car.

18:37.617 --> 18:39.118
Dumbass.

18:47.043 --> 18:49.086
Times are tough all over.

18:49.087 --> 18:51.964
But the true measure of a city

18:51.965 --> 18:54.758
is in how it responds to the hard times.

18:54.759 --> 18:58.178
And this isn't Topeka or Kalamazoo.

18:58.179 --> 18:59.680
This is New York.

18:59.681 --> 19:02.516
We're gonna link arms and stand strong

19:02.517 --> 19:05.185
against the rising tide.

19:05.186 --> 19:07.688
It was easy to stand up here
when the streets...

19:07.689 --> 19:10.065
What's the headline here?

19:10.066 --> 19:13.277
"Desperate Morris Delivers Dud."

19:13.278 --> 19:15.404
No, I'd-I'd go with quadruple M:

19:15.405 --> 19:17.573
"'Mayor's Missive Misses Mark."

19:17.574 --> 19:19.157
Man, I wouldn't trust Hudson

19:19.158 --> 19:22.327
to do my laundry and that man's
gonna beat Morris by ten points.

19:22.328 --> 19:25.831
Sometimes you just
want a different brand of snake oil.

19:25.832 --> 19:29.334
So, uh, you gonna explain your face?

19:29.335 --> 19:32.171
Let's just say you should
lay off the Addison reporting.

19:33.423 --> 19:35.007
Silvermane?

19:35.008 --> 19:38.093
He's on a warpath about Addison.
Wants to know who's coming after him.

19:38.094 --> 19:40.637
So tread... lightly.

19:40.638 --> 19:44.141
Man, I'm not the one with a face
that looks like hamburger meat.

19:44.142 --> 19:46.351
I've tangoed with his guys before.

19:46.352 --> 19:48.854
As the man with the mask and the goggles.

19:48.855 --> 19:51.648
New York's beloved hero of the hour.

19:51.649 --> 19:53.317
Not as Ben Reilly.

19:53.318 --> 19:54.818
You know what? Gimme that.

19:54.819 --> 19:56.904
I'm making a declaration right now.

19:56.905 --> 19:58.697
That's right.

19:58.698 --> 20:00.866
If I'm re-elected

20:00.867 --> 20:02.951
you can say goodbye to Prohibition.

20:02.952 --> 20:04.703
Man knows his audience.

20:04.704 --> 20:08.540
As God is my witness,
you'll never go thirsty again.

20:10.043 --> 20:13.170
Look, all I'm saying
is you're in it with Silvermane now.

20:13.171 --> 20:15.547
If the choice is to suit up or die,

20:15.548 --> 20:17.299
might be time to tango again.

20:17.300 --> 20:19.801
Maybe you'd be doing the city a favor
in the process.

20:19.802 --> 20:22.262
Oh, come on, Robbie. Enough of that.

20:22.263 --> 20:23.680
You know what I'm doing after this?

20:23.681 --> 20:25.557
- What?
- Being beautiful.

20:25.558 --> 20:28.727
And working the Addison story.

20:28.728 --> 20:31.314
I don't publish, I don't eat, my friend.

20:33.650 --> 20:35.652
I've been thinking about the Canadians.

20:36.903 --> 20:38.403
You gonna let me handle it?

20:38.404 --> 20:40.948
No, I'll do it.

20:40.949 --> 20:43.325
Plan stands, but...

20:43.326 --> 20:45.995
go ahead of me. Scout it out.

20:50.583 --> 20:52.459
Ah.

20:52.460 --> 20:54.503
I think it's stylish.

20:54.504 --> 20:56.089
What do you think, Winston?

20:57.173 --> 20:58.757
I'm not one for fashion.

20:58.758 --> 21:01.426
But the whole thing is a little...

21:01.427 --> 21:03.011
tired.

21:03.012 --> 21:06.182
Now, Winston,
have you got a gripe with her?

21:07.475 --> 21:11.311
No, I just think there's better things
to spend time on than dressing up dolls.

21:12.397 --> 21:14.856
Well, there's fashion and there's taste.

21:14.857 --> 21:18.610
Box it up. You like it too, right?

21:18.611 --> 21:19.820
Honestly, I think it's--

21:19.821 --> 21:21.531
Yeah, yeah, it's perfect.

21:40.091 --> 21:42.719
Excuse me, ma'am,
I'm looking for the Addisons.

21:55.690 --> 21:57.191
Mrs. Addison?

22:28.181 --> 22:29.682
Who are you?

22:34.520 --> 22:37.230
- Hey, brother.
- Don't "hey, brother" me.

22:37.231 --> 22:38.857
I asked you a question.

22:38.858 --> 22:40.150
You sure did,

22:40.151 --> 22:43.028
and seeing as you are a very large

22:43.029 --> 22:44.571
- and angry man,
- Mm.

22:44.572 --> 22:45.822
I'm gonna answer.

22:45.823 --> 22:47.657
I'm looking for Vera Addison.

22:47.658 --> 22:49.618
Know where she is?

22:49.619 --> 22:50.994
Why do you want to know?

22:50.995 --> 22:52.871
Well, I am a reporter.

22:52.872 --> 22:54.998
Working a story on James Addison's death.

22:54.999 --> 22:57.418
Wanted to talk to his widow.

23:00.171 --> 23:01.672
Jimmy's dead?

23:04.217 --> 23:06.677
Oh, I'm sorry.
You... you guys were friends?

23:07.845 --> 23:09.347
How did he die?

23:10.431 --> 23:11.933
Mm, there was an explosion...

23:13.976 --> 23:16.269
...at the Standard Oil depot.

23:16.270 --> 23:18.021
Why are you writing about him?

23:18.022 --> 23:21.191
Well, before he died
he burned down the wrong house.

23:21.192 --> 23:22.776
Whose?

23:22.777 --> 23:24.278
Silvermane.

23:32.620 --> 23:33.829
- Think it's time for you to leave.
- Wait, wait,

23:33.830 --> 23:35.455
wait, wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait.

23:35.456 --> 23:37.332
Addison didn't just take it

23:37.333 --> 23:40.293
upon himself to burn down the house
of the most dangerous man in the city.

23:40.294 --> 23:42.045
Someone paid him to do it.

23:42.046 --> 23:45.590
Now, look, he was your friend,
so I'm guessing he wasn't a bad guy.

23:45.591 --> 23:47.134
He was sick.

23:47.135 --> 23:50.679
And these days call for men
to use their sicknesses to get by.

23:50.680 --> 23:53.140
Until their sicknesses eat them alive.

23:53.141 --> 23:55.601
- Hang on, what do you mean, he was sick?
- I don't know who hired him.

23:57.061 --> 23:58.812
But, yeah,

23:58.813 --> 24:00.355
his wife might.

24:00.356 --> 24:02.065
And do you know where I can find her?

24:02.066 --> 24:03.817
Try the Geoffrey Hotel.

24:03.818 --> 24:05.944
She always went there
when they came into some money.

24:05.945 --> 24:07.654
And when she came back,

24:07.655 --> 24:09.281
the money was gone.

24:09.282 --> 24:10.991
Go figure.

24:10.992 --> 24:13.326
Well, thanks.

24:13.327 --> 24:14.829
I'll pay her a visit.

24:17.832 --> 24:19.958
I told you,

24:19.959 --> 24:21.918
he hardly comes to the office anymore.

24:21.919 --> 24:23.879
I can't remember the last time I saw him.

24:23.880 --> 24:27.215
Well, maybe this'll jog your memory.

24:27.216 --> 24:29.217
Please! I'm telling you the truth.

24:31.304 --> 24:33.597
For your sake, I hope so.

24:33.598 --> 24:35.348
We'll be back.

24:50.489 --> 24:51.489
Janet!

24:51.490 --> 24:53.159
Did they hurt you?

24:54.368 --> 24:57.621
No, not this time.
But they said they'd be back.

24:58.915 --> 25:01.374
Ben, they put a gun to my head.

25:01.375 --> 25:03.335
They kept saying that
I'd end up like Donegal?

25:03.336 --> 25:05.879
That if I didn't tell them where you were,

25:05.880 --> 25:08.882
he and I'd be crossing
the River Styx together.

25:08.883 --> 25:10.718
What does that mean?

25:11.969 --> 25:13.887
It means Donegal's dead.

25:13.888 --> 25:15.972
Silvermane killed him.

25:15.973 --> 25:17.933
But I'll take care of it.

25:17.934 --> 25:21.728
Ever since Ruby died, I've been waiting
for you to get it back together.

25:21.729 --> 25:25.023
Back to the man I know
is buried somewhere inside you.

25:25.024 --> 25:26.692
Five years.

25:28.236 --> 25:29.946
And this is how it ends.

25:31.030 --> 25:32.572
Janet.

25:32.573 --> 25:34.282
Go home. Get-get some rest.

25:34.283 --> 25:36.911
You'll feel better and I'll…
I'll call you when it's safe.

25:37.995 --> 25:39.497
Yeah, I'm gonna go home.

25:41.207 --> 25:42.791
But I am not coming back.

25:42.792 --> 25:45.543
I care about you, Ben,

25:45.544 --> 25:47.046
so deeply.

25:48.297 --> 25:50.299
But not enough to die for you.

25:51.509 --> 25:52.718
Janet...

25:53.803 --> 25:56.305
Janet!

26:44.478 --> 26:46.313
Hiya! I'm Pete with Maintenance.

26:46.314 --> 26:48.148
Sorry about the leak.
It'll be no problem.

26:48.149 --> 26:50.400
I'll just, uh-- Gosh, the unit downstairs,

26:50.401 --> 26:52.402
big mess. Water, water everywhere.

26:52.403 --> 26:54.112
- What's going on?
- Something about a leak?

26:54.113 --> 26:56.990
Oh, I like what you've done with place.
Although if you move the table

26:56.991 --> 27:00.535
over by the window,
you really get that sunset glow at dinner.

27:00.536 --> 27:02.996
- I told you that.
- I'm sorry, have you been here before?

27:02.997 --> 27:06.834
I am familiar with the unit, yes.
Uh, bathroom's that way, hmm?

27:25.978 --> 27:28.396
Well, don't just stand there.
Say something.

27:28.397 --> 27:31.484
Um, sir, w-what exactly are you fixing?

27:32.318 --> 27:34.319
Uh, yep, yeah, I found the issue.

27:34.320 --> 27:36.988
You've got a busted gerry casket.

27:36.989 --> 27:38.948
It's a misalignment

27:38.949 --> 27:41.285
from the mission joist.

28:03.516 --> 28:05.726
Excuse me,
w-what's happening in there?

28:06.894 --> 28:09.397
Bit of an existential crisis,
if I'm honest.

28:11.190 --> 28:13.025
About my toilet?

28:29.959 --> 28:31.794
I don't think that guy was a plumber.

28:54.024 --> 28:55.651
Stairs are to the left.

28:57.319 --> 28:58.821
Thanks for your trouble.

29:00.823 --> 29:02.616
Thanks for the dollar.

29:04.910 --> 29:06.745
Mrs. Addison?

29:09.290 --> 29:10.874
I didn't order anything.

29:10.875 --> 29:13.543
My name is Robbie Robertson.
I'm a reporter.

29:13.544 --> 29:17.088
Hold-hold-- ho-hold on,
hold on now, I just...

29:17.089 --> 29:18.673
- I just want to talk.
- You got three seconds

29:18.674 --> 29:20.758
to get out of here or I'm gonna scream.

29:20.759 --> 29:22.594
And I don't think you want
a white woman screaming

29:22.595 --> 29:25.097
about a Black man trying
to force his way into her hotel room.

29:26.682 --> 29:28.975
Actually, I got a hunch...

29:28.976 --> 29:31.352
that you wouldn't want
the city's most ruthless gangster

29:31.353 --> 29:35.190
knowing that the money someone
paid your husband to kill him

29:35.191 --> 29:37.275
was being spent on...

29:37.276 --> 29:40.320
lobster and designer clothes.

29:40.321 --> 29:43.364
So, go ahead and scream, honey.
Unless you want me to do it.

29:43.365 --> 29:45.950
I got a pretty deep voice.
It really carries.

30:08.516 --> 30:10.099
So, that's it?

30:10.100 --> 30:11.935
What do you mean?

30:11.936 --> 30:15.104
No tears?
I just told you your husband died.

30:15.105 --> 30:17.316
People grieve in different ways.

30:19.109 --> 30:21.278
You already knew.

30:22.780 --> 30:26.366
James was a lot of things,
but not the type to cut and run.

30:26.367 --> 30:29.786
When he didn't come home that night,
I figured he was never coming home.

30:29.787 --> 30:32.580
- When did he start setting fires?
- Six months ago.

30:32.581 --> 30:35.291
Suddenly discovered
he had an innate talent for it.

30:35.292 --> 30:36.919
Who hired him for the Silvermane job?

30:38.170 --> 30:41.381
Just because I didn't scream
doesn't mean I'm an open book.

30:41.382 --> 30:43.508
As far as I'm concerned,

30:43.509 --> 30:46.177
James dug his own grave
and now he's lying in it.

31:02.820 --> 31:04.737
This place feels haunted.

31:04.738 --> 31:06.532
That's 'cause it is.

31:08.576 --> 31:10.911
Speaking of ghosts...

31:12.496 --> 31:14.038
...Jimmy Addison's dead.

31:14.039 --> 31:15.541
What?

31:16.709 --> 31:17.959
When?

31:17.960 --> 31:20.169
Couple days ago.
Some reporter came around

31:20.170 --> 31:23.423
asking about him. Wanted to know
who hired him to kill Silvermane.

31:27.094 --> 31:28.177
You didn't know.

31:28.178 --> 31:30.598
If I'd known, I would have stopped him.

31:39.106 --> 31:40.648
Flint.

31:40.649 --> 31:42.109
You don't look so good.

31:43.193 --> 31:45.403
It happened again.

31:45.404 --> 31:47.363
I changed completely this time.

31:47.364 --> 31:49.032
Never changed back.

31:49.033 --> 31:50.784
Eh, not all the way.

31:52.202 --> 31:54.121
It's like the doc said.

31:55.289 --> 31:56.957
Our clocks are ticking.

31:58.751 --> 32:00.627
Faster and faster now.

32:00.628 --> 32:02.504
Everything we went through.

32:05.215 --> 32:07.675
We deserve better, you and I.

32:07.676 --> 32:09.260
Let's get out of here.

32:09.261 --> 32:11.346
You can crash at my place.

32:11.347 --> 32:14.015
Better for us to stick together right now.

32:15.976 --> 32:17.645
Yeah.

32:18.520 --> 32:21.856
You have to check every crate?
Is it 'cause we're Canadians?

32:21.857 --> 32:24.275
Yeah, it's 'cause
you're Canadian. No.

32:24.276 --> 32:27.153
Boss doesn't trust anyone.
Myself included.

32:27.154 --> 32:29.989
That's why he still runs this town.

32:29.990 --> 32:31.824
Shipment's good, boss.

32:31.825 --> 32:33.242
Ready for you to come.

32:33.243 --> 32:35.703
Right. I'm on my way.

33:07.736 --> 33:09.947
What is that?

33:16.286 --> 33:17.829
Hey, go check it out.

33:17.830 --> 33:20.123
Go. Go, go, go, go, go!

33:21.208 --> 33:23.167
He's on the roof! Aah!

33:27.965 --> 33:28.882
Shoot him!

33:40.269 --> 33:41.645
Hello.

34:00.873 --> 34:02.124
Where'd he go?

34:09.923 --> 34:11.133
That way.

34:13.761 --> 34:15.220
Come here!

34:16.263 --> 34:17.765
Thank you.

34:18.724 --> 34:20.142
Oh! God.

34:21.143 --> 34:22.519
Don't you ever run out of bullets?

34:23.228 --> 34:24.729
Guess you do.

34:24.730 --> 34:26.564
Huh?

34:34.239 --> 34:36.825
What? What the hell are you waiting for?

34:37.910 --> 34:39.494
After you.

34:39.495 --> 34:41.454
No, no. By all means.

34:41.455 --> 34:42.747
Out of the car!

34:52.132 --> 34:54.009
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa! Not another step.

34:58.138 --> 35:00.015
See? Tai chi.

35:12.402 --> 35:14.779
- It's been a while.
- You've done well

35:14.780 --> 35:17.073
without me around, haven't you?

35:17.074 --> 35:19.242
Didn't know you did hit jobs now.

35:19.243 --> 35:22.620
- Do you mind if I ask you who hired you?
- Nobody hires me.

35:22.621 --> 35:24.456
I'm here because of Ben Reilly.

35:25.415 --> 35:28.835
- Reilly? The flatfoot?
- Yeah, that's right. I owe him a favor.

35:28.836 --> 35:30.586
Sorry, where are my manners?

35:30.587 --> 35:32.964
- Do you want a drink?
- No. I want you and your goons

35:32.965 --> 35:34.507
to lay off Reilly.

35:34.508 --> 35:36.425
He doesn't know who tried to kill you

35:36.426 --> 35:39.929
and roughing up his secretary
isn't gonna change that.

35:39.930 --> 35:43.140
So, I leave the gumshoe alone,
and that's it?

35:43.141 --> 35:45.101
'Cause, you know,
back in the day you really

35:45.102 --> 35:48.604
- couldn't leave me alone, could you?
- I don't think you're listening to me,

35:48.605 --> 35:50.439
Silvermane.

35:50.440 --> 35:52.358
This is your only warning.

35:52.359 --> 35:53.734
If you mess with Reilly

35:53.735 --> 35:55.237
or any of his people…

35:56.989 --> 35:58.490
...I will kill you.

36:49.416 --> 36:50.416
Reilly.

36:50.417 --> 36:52.627
This you? This your doing?

36:52.628 --> 36:54.170
What are you talking about?

36:54.171 --> 36:56.464
Did you stop Silvermane's car?

36:56.465 --> 36:57.882
Oh, you heard about that, huh?

36:57.883 --> 36:59.634
Yeah, well, I got some bad news for you.

36:59.635 --> 37:02.011
Cops had an ambush
set up for Silvermane at the docks.

37:02.012 --> 37:04.221
Someone gave them a tip
about a booze exchange.

37:04.222 --> 37:07.475
Someone tipped off the cops
about a Silvermane booze exchange?

37:07.476 --> 37:09.810
Yeah, they're rounding up
about a dozen of his guys right now.

37:09.811 --> 37:11.687
Cops were all set to catch
the man himself in the act.

37:11.688 --> 37:13.272
But Silvermane never showed.

37:13.273 --> 37:15.816
Do they know why he didn't show?

37:15.817 --> 37:19.612
No, don't worry. Police got word that
someone stopped Silvermane from coming.

37:19.613 --> 37:21.197
They don't know it was you.

37:21.198 --> 37:24.158
Shit, got to go.
I ain't trying to die in no phone booth.

37:50.852 --> 37:52.854
What the hell did I just do?

37:57.109 --> 37:59.110
♪ Now ♪

37:59.111 --> 38:02.114
♪ you say you're lonely ♪

38:05.492 --> 38:07.118
♪ Said you cried ♪

38:07.119 --> 38:10.204
♪ the whole night through ♪

38:10.205 --> 38:12.331
♪ Well you can ♪

38:12.332 --> 38:14.501
♪ cry me a river ♪

38:15.961 --> 38:18.046
♪ Cry me a river ♪

38:20.007 --> 38:23.927
♪ 'cause I cried a river over you ♪

38:25.345 --> 38:27.848
♪ Ooh ♪

38:28.056 --> 38:31.977
♪ And now you say you're sorry ♪

38:34.354 --> 38:38.233
♪ for being so untrue ♪

38:40.736 --> 38:42.528
♪ So what? ♪

38:42.529 --> 38:44.990
♪ Just cry me a river ♪

38:46.033 --> 38:48.118
♪ Cry me a river ♪

38:50.245 --> 38:54.166
♪ I cried a river over you ♪

38:57.044 --> 38:58.419
♪ You drove me ♪

38:58.420 --> 39:01.756
♪ nearly drove me out of my head ♪

39:01.757 --> 39:05.676
♪ Bye-bye, my love ♪

39:05.677 --> 39:09.388
♪ while you never shed a tear ♪

39:09.389 --> 39:11.766
♪ Bye-bye, my love ♪

39:11.767 --> 39:14.393
♪ Remember? ♪

39:14.394 --> 39:16.896
♪ I remember all you said ♪

39:16.897 --> 39:18.689
♪ Bye-bye, my love ♪

39:18.690 --> 39:21.859
♪ Told me love was too plebeian ♪

39:21.860 --> 39:25.571
♪ Told me you were through with me ♪

39:25.572 --> 39:28.491
♪ And now you say ♪

39:28.492 --> 39:30.494
♪ you love me ♪

39:32.996 --> 39:36.540
♪ Well, just to prove ♪

39:36.541 --> 39:38.168
♪ you do ♪

39:39.377 --> 39:42.922
♪ go on and cry me a river ♪

39:42.923 --> 39:46.510
♪ I'd like to see you cry a river ♪

39:48.553 --> 39:51.639
♪ 'cause I'm tired ♪

39:51.640 --> 39:56.227
♪ of crying over ♪

39:56.228 --> 40:00.607
♪ you ♪
